                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number">Q4</span>
                    <div class="eq-question">Explain desired-vs-actual state using a <code>replicas: 3</code> example.</div>
                    <details>
                        <summary>Show Answer</summary>
                        <div class="eq-answer-label">Answer</div>
                        <p><strong>Desired</strong> = what you declared (<code>replicas: 3</code>, stored in etcd). <strong>Actual</strong> = what's really running on the nodes. A controller continuously diffs them: if actual is 2, it creates one pod; if actual is 4, it deletes one.</p>
                        <table>
                            <thead><tr><th>Diff (desired = 3)</th><th>Controller acts</th></tr></thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr><td>actual &lt; 3</td><td>CREATE the missing pod(s)</td></tr>
                                <tr><td>actual &gt; 3</td><td>DELETE the extra pod(s)</td></tr>
                                <tr><td>actual = 3</td><td>do nothing (idempotent — no churn)</td></tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                        <div class="eq-explanation">
                            <div class="eq-exp-label">Explanation</div>
                            <p>This gap-closing loop is the core mental model for the whole exam. Troubleshooting = "find where actual diverged from desired, and why the controller can't close the gap."</p>
                        </div>
                    </details>
                </div>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number">Q5</span>
                    <div class="eq-question">List three tasks that belong to the CKA but NOT the CKAD.</div>
