                        <summary>Show Answer</summary>
                        <div class="eq-answer-label">Answer</div>
                        <p>Any three of: install a cluster with <strong>kubeadm</strong>; <strong>etcd</strong> backup &amp; restore; approve/rotate <strong>certificates</strong> (PKI); <strong>cluster upgrades</strong>; <strong>node management</strong> (drain/cordon); configure <strong>CNI/CoreDNS</strong>.</p>
                        <table>
                            <thead><tr><th>🔧 CKA owns (below the app)</th><th>👩‍💻 CKAD owns (the app)</th></tr></thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr><td>kubeadm install · etcd backup/restore</td><td>Pods · Deployments</td></tr>
                                <tr><td>certificates / PKI · cluster upgrades</td><td>Services · ConfigMaps</td></tr>
                                <tr><td>node drain / cordon · CNI / CoreDNS</td><td>probes · resource limits</td></tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                        <div class="eq-explanation">
                            <div class="eq-exp-label">Explanation</div>
                            <p>All are <em>below the app</em>. CKAD stays at the workload layer (Pods/Deployments/Services/ConfigMaps); CKA owns the infrastructure those run on.</p>
                        </div>
