   --kubeconfig=FILE          ◀── highest — explicit flag on this one command
        │  not passed?
        ▼
   $KUBECONFIG=a:b:c          ◀── merged list of files, first definition of a key wins
        │  not set?
        ▼
   ~/.kube/config             ◀── lowest — the default, used when nothing else is set
</pre>
                        <div class="eq-explanation"><div class="eq-exp-label">Explanation</div><p>So a stray <code>$KUBECONFIG</code> in your shell silently overrides the default file — a classic "why can't I see my cluster?" gotcha.</p></div>
