            <div class="cka-practice-drill">
                <h4>🔬 Practice Drill 5.3 — The Pre-Flight Health Sweep (Never Deploy Blind)</h4>
                <div class="drill-timer">⏱️ Target Time: 5 minutes</div>
                <div class="drill-scenario">
                    <h5>Scenario</h5>
                    <p>You've just been handed a cluster (context <code>minikube</code>). Before deploying easypj, run the full health sweep: API reachable → nodes Ready → system pods Running → DNS resolving. One check must use a <em>throwaway pod</em>. State what "healthy" looks like for each step.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="drill-hint">
                    <strong>Hint:</strong> Four commands, in dependency order: <code>cluster-info</code> → <code>get nodes</code> → <code>get pods -n kube-system</code> → a busybox <code>nslookup kubernetes.default</code>. Any failure invalidates everything after it.
                </div>
                <div class="drill-solution">
                    <details>
                        <summary>View Solution</summary>
                        <div class="code-block-wrapper">
                            <div class="code-block-header"><span class="code-dot red"></span><span class="code-dot yellow"></span><span class="code-dot green"></span><span class="code-lang">the 4-step sweep</span></div>
<pre><code class="language-bash"><span class="comment"># 0. Right cluster first — always</span>
kubectl config use-context minikube

<span class="comment"># 1. Is the API server even reachable?</span>
kubectl cluster-info                 <span class="comment"># control plane + CoreDNS URLs print ✅</span>

<span class="comment"># 2. Are all nodes Ready?</span>
kubectl get nodes                    <span class="comment"># every STATUS = Ready ✅</span>

<span class="comment"># 3. Is the system layer healthy?</span>
kubectl get pods -n kube-system      <span class="comment"># coredns/etcd/apiserver/kube-proxy Running ✅</span>

<span class="comment"># 4. Does cluster DNS actually resolve? (throwaway pod, auto-cleans)</span>
kubectl run tmp --image=busybox:1.28 --rm -it --restart=Never -- \
  nslookup kubernetes.default        <span class="comment"># resolves to the API Service VIP ✅</span></code></pre>
                        </div>
                        <table>
                            <thead><tr><th>Step fails?</th><th>It means</th></tr></thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr><td>① cluster-info</td><td>wrong context / API server down — nothing else matters yet</td></tr>
                                <tr><td>② a node NotReady</td><td>kubelet / CNI / runtime on that node (Ch 3 order)</td></tr>
                                <tr><td>③ CoreDNS CrashLoop</td><td>DNS will fail cluster-wide — fix before deploying</td></tr>
                                <tr><td>④ nslookup fails</td><td>DNS/network path broken even though pods run — CNI or CoreDNS config</td></tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                        <p><strong>Check yourself:</strong> the sweep is ordered by <em>dependency</em> — each step assumes the previous one passed. Skipping it and deploying anyway is how you end up debugging phantom "application bugs" that are really a broken control plane. Make it a ritual: new cluster → 4-step sweep → then work.</p>
                    </details>
                </div>
            </div>

