                        4. Uncordon and verify</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="code-block-wrapper">
                    <div class="code-block-header">
                        <span class="code-dot red"></span>
                        <span class="code-dot yellow"></span>
                        <span class="code-dot green"></span>
                        <span class="code-lang">Exercise 14.1 — Solution (try it yourself first!)</span>
                    </div>
<pre><code class="language-bash"><span class="comment"># 1. Taint the node</span>
kubectl taint node node01 env=prod:NoSchedule

<span class="comment"># 2. Create nginx pod (no toleration)</span>
kubectl run nginx-test --image=nginx
kubectl get pod nginx-test -o wide
<span class="comment"># → Should be on a different node (not node01)</span>

<span class="comment"># 3. Create pod WITH toleration</span>
cat &lt;&lt;'EOF' | kubectl apply -f -
apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: nginx-tolerant
spec:
  tolerations:
  - key: "env"
    operator: "Equal"
    value: "prod"
    effect: "NoSchedule"
  containers:
  - name: nginx
    image: nginx
EOF
kubectl get pod nginx-tolerant -o wide
<span class="comment"># → Can schedule on node01</span>

<span class="comment"># 4. Remove taint</span>
kubectl taint node node01 env=prod:NoSchedule-

<span class="comment"># Clean up</span>
kubectl delete pod nginx-test nginx-tolerant</code></pre>
                </div>
            </section>
            <!-- ─────────── UNDER THE HOOD ─────────── -->
            <span class="ch-jump" id="ch14-uth"></span>
            <details class="uth"><summary>Under the Hood — How the Scheduler Filters and Scores Nodes: Filtering Plugins, Scoring Algorithms, Taints/Tolerations, and Node Affinity Resolution</summary>
            <div class="uth-body">
            <h5>🗺️ The Scheduling Pipeline — Two-Phase Decision Making</h5>
            <p>The kube-scheduler doesn't randomly assign pods. It runs a sophisticated two-phase algorithm: FILTERING (eliminate infeasible nodes) → SCORING (rank remaining nodes). Understanding this helps you debug "0/3 nodes are available" errors.</p>
            <div class="uth-diagram"><pre>
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  SCHEDULING PIPELINE — Full Algorithm                                        │
│                                                                              │
│  Pod to schedule: easypj-web (requests: cpu=500m, memory=512Mi)             │
│  Cluster: 5 worker nodes                                                      │
│                                                                              │
│  ═══════════════════ PHASE 1: FILTERING (5 nodes → ?) ═══════════════════    │
│  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐    │
│  │ FILTER PLUGIN          CHECK                   N1  N2  N3  N4  N5   │    │
│  │ ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────  │    │
│  │ NodeUnschedulable      node.spec.unschedulable?  ✅  ✅  ✅  ✅  ✅   │    │
│  │ NodeResourcesFit       enough cpu/memory?       ✅  ✅  ❌  ✅  ✅   │    │
│  │                         (N3: only 200m cpu free)                      │    │
│  │ NodeSelector           node labels match?        ✅  ✅  -   ✅  ✅   │    │
│  │ NodeAffinity           affinity rules match?     ✅  ✅  -   ✅  ✅   │    │
│  │ TaintToleration        pod tolerates taints?    ✅  ❌  -   ✅  ✅   │    │
│  │                         (N2: taint gpu=true:NoSchedule)               │    │
│  │ NodePorts              hostPort conflicts?       ✅  -   -   ✅  ✅   │    │
│  │ VolumeLimits           can attach more volumes?  ✅  -   -   ✅  ✅   │    │
│  │                                                                      │    │
│  │ FILTERED: 3 nodes survive (N1, N4, N5)                               │    │
│  │ ELIMINATED: N2 (taint), N3 (insufficient resources)                  │    │
│  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘    │
│                                                                              │
│  ═══════════════════ PHASE 2: SCORING (3 nodes → ranking) ═══════════════    │
│  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐    │
│  │ SCORING PLUGIN          WEIGHT     N1     N4     N5    DESCRIPTION   │    │
│  │ ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────  │    │
│  │ NodeResourcesFit        1.0        85     72     90    Least loaded  │    │
│  │   (LeastAllocated)                                   wins (N5)      │    │
│  │ NodeResourcesBalanced   1.0        78     88     65    Balanced CPU  │    │
│  │   (BalancedAllocation)                               /memory (N4)   │    │
│  │ ImageLocality           1.0        90     50     50    Image cached  │    │
│  │   (image already on node)                             on N1?         │    │
│  │ NodeAffinityPriority    1.0        100    50     50    Preferred     │    │
│  │   (preferredDuringScheduling)                        affinity (N1)  │    │
│  │ InterPodAffinity        2.0        50     100    50    Pods with     │    │
│  │   (preferredDuringScheduling)                        same affinity  │    │
│  │                                                      on N4          │    │
