                        <li>Create a CronJob <code>easypj-slow-backup</code> that sleeps for 90s, firing every minute (<code>* * * * *</code>)</li>
                        <li>Set <code>concurrencyPolicy: Forbid</code> and watch <code>kubectl get jobs -w</code> — confirm ticks are SKIPPED, not queued, while the previous run is still active</li>
                        <li>Change to <code>concurrencyPolicy: Replace</code> — confirm the still-running Job is killed when the next tick fires</li>
                        <li>Explain what <code>startingDeadlineSeconds: 30</code> would do if the controller-manager were down for 2 minutes</li>
                    </ol>
                </div>
                <div class="drill-hint">
                    <strong>Hint:</strong> with <code>Forbid</code>, a skipped tick is gone forever — it is NOT queued up and run later once the previous Job finishes.
                </div>
                <div class="drill-solution">
                    <details>
                        <summary>View Solution</summary>
                        <pre><code class="language-bash">cat &lt;&lt;EOF | kubectl apply -f -
apiVersion: batch/v1
kind: CronJob
metadata:
  name: easypj-slow-backup
spec:
  schedule: "* * * * *"
  concurrencyPolicy: Forbid
  jobTemplate:
    spec:
      template:
        spec:
          restartPolicy: OnFailure
          containers:
          - name: slow
            image: busybox
            command: ["sh","-c","sleep 90"]
EOF

kubectl get jobs -w   <span class="comment"># ticks at minute+1 are skipped while the 90s job is still running</span>

kubectl patch cronjob easypj-slow-backup -p '{"spec":{"concurrencyPolicy":"Replace"}}'
kubectl get jobs -w   <span class="comment"># the running job is now killed and replaced at the next tick</span>

<span class="comment"># startingDeadlineSeconds:30 -&gt; if the controller was down &gt;30s past a scheduled</span>
<span class="comment"># tick, that tick is counted as MISSED and never launched at all, instead of</span>
<span class="comment"># being launched late when the controller comes back.</span></code></pre>
                    </details>
                </div>
            </div>

