                <div class="scenario-box">
                    <h5>🧪 CKA Practice Scenario: Network Debugging</h5>
                    <p><strong>Situation:</strong> A junior admin reports that the easypj Django app can't connect to the postgres database. Pods are Running, but <code>curl http://postgres-svc:5432</code> from the easypj pod times out.</p>
                    <div class="code-block-wrapper">
                        <div class="code-block-header">
                            <span class="code-dot red"></span>
                            <span class="code-dot yellow"></span>
                            <span class="code-dot green"></span>
                            <span class="code-lang">Step-by-Step Diagnosis</span>
                        </div>
<pre><code class="language-bash"><span class="comment"># Step 1: Can DNS resolve the service name?</span>
kubectl exec easypj-pod -- nslookup postgres-svc
<span class="comment"># ✅ Returns 10.96.88.5 — DNS is fine</span>

<span class="comment"># Step 2: Can we reach the pod directly by IP?</span>
kubectl get pods -o wide | grep postgres
<span class="comment"># postgres-0   10.244.2.8   worker-2</span>
kubectl exec easypj-pod -- nc -zv 10.244.2.8 5432
<span class="comment"># ✅ open — pod-to-pod networking works</span>

<span class="comment"># Step 3: Can we reach the SERVICE IP?</span>
kubectl exec easypj-pod -- nc -zv 10.96.88.5 5432
<span class="comment"># ❌ TIMEOUT — Service routing is broken!</span>

<span class="comment"># Step 4: Check kube-proxy</span>
kubectl get pods -n kube-system -l k8s-app=kube-proxy
<span class="comment"># kube-proxy-abc12  0/1  CrashLoopBackOff  ← FOUND IT!</span>

