            <div class="uth-body">
            <h5>🗺️ The 4 Fundamental Kubernetes Networking Rules</h5>
            <p>Kubernetes networking is built on a flat, routable pod network. Every pod gets its own IP, and pods on different nodes communicate without NAT. The CNI plugin implements this, and kube-proxy handles Services on top.</p>
