            <span class="ch-jump" id="ch18-uth"></span>
            <details class="uth"><summary>Under the Hood — How kube-proxy Programs iptables/IPVS for Service Load Balancing: Complete Packet Flow from Client Pod to Backend Pod via ClusterIP</summary>
            <div class="uth-body">
            <h5>🗺️ Service Traffic Flow — From Client to Backend via ClusterIP</h5>
            <p>When a pod sends traffic to a Service ClusterIP (virtual IP), kube-proxy's iptables rules redirect it to a real pod IP. This is NOT a proxy — the kernel does it at wire speed with netfilter rules.</p>
            <div class="uth-diagram"><pre>
