                <div class="scenario-box">
                    <h5>🧪 CKA Practice Scenario: DNS Broken After Cluster Upgrade</h5>
                    <p><strong>Situation:</strong> After upgrading to K8s 1.29, pods report <code>nslookup: can't resolve 'easypj-svc'</code>. The CoreDNS pods are stuck in <code>CrashLoopBackOff</code>.</p>
                    <div class="code-block-wrapper">
                        <div class="code-block-header">
                            <span class="code-dot red"></span>
                            <span class="code-dot yellow"></span>
                            <span class="code-dot green"></span>
                            <span class="code-lang">Step-by-Step DNS Recovery</span>
                        </div>
<pre><code class="language-bash"><span class="comment"># Step 1: Confirm CoreDNS is crashing</span>
kubectl get pods -n kube-system -l k8s-app=kube-dns
<span class="comment"># coredns-abc-111  0/1  CrashLoopBackOff  5 (2m ago)</span>
<span class="comment"># coredns-abc-222  0/1  CrashLoopBackOff  5 (2m ago)</span>

<span class="comment"># Step 2: Check logs for the error</span>
kubectl logs -n kube-system coredns-abc-111
<span class="comment"># "Loop (127.0.0.1:43522 -> :53) detected for zone '.'"</span>
<span class="comment"># ← DNS forwarding loop!</span>

<span class="comment"># Step 3: The cause — node's /etc/resolv.conf points to</span>
<span class="comment"># 127.0.0.53 (systemd-resolved), which forwards back to CoreDNS</span>
<span class="comment"># This creates a loop!</span>

<span class="comment"># Step 4: Fix the Corefile — replace /etc/resolv.conf with</span>
<span class="comment"># explicit upstream DNS servers</span>
kubectl edit configmap coredns -n kube-system
<span class="comment"># Change:  forward . /etc/resolv.conf</span>
<span class="comment"># To:      forward . 8.8.8.8 8.8.4.4</span>

<span class="comment"># Step 5: Wait for auto-reload (30s) or delete pods to force restart</span>
kubectl delete pods -n kube-system -l k8s-app=kube-dns

<span class="comment"># Step 6: Verify DNS is working again</span>
kubectl run dnscheck --image=busybox --rm -it -- nslookup easypj-svc
<span class="comment"># Address: 10.96.45.2  ✅ Fixed!</span></code></pre>
                    </div>
                </div>
