                            <div class="eq-exp-label">Explanation</div>
                            <p><code>kubernetes.default</code> is the built-in Service that points to the API server. It always exists in every cluster. If <code>nslookup kubernetes.default</code> works, DNS is functioning. If it fails, CoreDNS is broken. On the CKA, this one-liner is your go-to DNS test. Prefer <code>busybox:1.28</code> specifically — newer busybox images ship a flaky musl-libc resolver that can give false-negative <code>nslookup</code> results, making a healthy cluster look broken. The <code>--rm -it --restart=Never</code> flags create a temporary pod that's cleaned up after use.</p>
