                    <h5>Scenario</h5>
                    <ol>
                        <li>Create a pod with a <code>hostPath</code> volume pointing at a directory that does NOT yet exist on the node, using <code>type: Directory</code> (the strict form)</li>
                        <li>Confirm the pod gets stuck in <code>ContainerCreating</code></li>
                        <li>Read the exact error from <code>kubectl describe pod</code>'s Events</li>
                        <li>Fix it by switching to <code>type: DirectoryOrCreate</code>, and confirm the pod now starts</li>
                    </ol>
                </div>
                <div class="drill-hint">
                    <strong>Hint:</strong> the fix is a ONE-WORD change (<code>Directory</code> → <code>DirectoryOrCreate</code>) — resist the urge to manually create the directory on the node first, since that's not how the exam or a real GitOps workflow would expect you to solve it.
                </div>
                <div class="drill-solution">
                    <details>
                        <summary>View Solution</summary>
                        <pre><code class="language-bash">kubectl apply -f - &lt;&lt;'EOF'
apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata: {name: hostpath-broken}
spec:
  containers:
  - {name: app, image: busybox, command: ["sleep","3600"], volumeMounts: [{name: v, mountPath: /data}]}
  volumes:
  - {name: v, hostPath: {path: /opt/does-not-exist-yet, type: Directory}}
EOF

kubectl get pod hostpath-broken   <span class="comment"># ContainerCreating, stuck</span>
kubectl describe pod hostpath-broken | grep -A2 Events
<span class="comment"># Warning FailedMount ... hostPath type check failed: /opt/does-not-exist-yet is not a directory</span>

<span class="comment"># A pod's volumes[] field is immutable after creation — patching it in place</span>
<span class="comment"># is rejected. Delete and recreate with the fix instead:</span>
kubectl delete pod hostpath-broken
kubectl apply -f - &lt;&lt;'EOF'
apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata: {name: hostpath-broken}
spec:
  containers:
  - {name: app, image: busybox, command: ["sleep","3600"], volumeMounts: [{name: v, mountPath: /data}]}
  volumes:
  - {name: v, hostPath: {path: /opt/does-not-exist-yet, type: DirectoryOrCreate}}
EOF

kubectl get pod hostpath-broken   <span class="comment"># Running — DirectoryOrCreate auto-created the missing path</span></code></pre>
                    </details>
                </div>
            </div>

