                </div>

                <!-- Critical Warning: Base64 is NOT encryption -->
                <div class="info-box warning">
                    <h5>⚠️ Base64 is NOT Encryption!</h5>
                    <p>Kubernetes Secrets are <strong>base64 encoded, NOT encrypted</strong> by default. Anyone with <code>kubectl get secret -o yaml</code> access can decode them instantly. Base64 is just encoding — like translating English to pig Latin. It provides <strong>zero security</strong> on its own.</p>
