                    <div class="eq-question">How do you create a Secret from a certificate file? Show creating a TLS Secret and verifying it.</div>
                    <details>
                        <summary>Show Answer</summary>
                            <div class="eq-answer-label">Answer</div>
                            <div class="code-block-wrapper">
                                <div class="code-block-header"><span class="code-dot red"></span><span class="code-dot yellow"></span><span class="code-dot green"></span><span class="code-lang">create tls secret from cert and key files</span></div>
                            <pre><code class="language-bash"><span class="comment"># Create TLS Secret from cert and key files:</span>
kubectl create secret tls app-tls \
--cert=server.crt \
--key=server.key

<span class="comment"># Verify:</span>
kubectl get secret app-tls -o yaml
<span class="comment"># type: kubernetes.io/tls</span>
<span class="comment"># data:</span>
<span class="comment">#   tls.crt: LS0tLS1CRUd...   ← base64 of cert</span>
<span class="comment">#   tls.key: LS0tLS1CRUd...   ← base64 of key</span>

<span class="comment"># Decode and inspect the certificate:</span>
kubectl get secret app-tls \
-o jsonpath='{.data.tls\.crt}' | base64 -d | openssl x509 -text -noout
<span class="comment"># Subject: CN = myapp.example.com</span>
<span class="comment"># Issuer: ...</span>
<span class="comment"># Validity: ...</span>

<span class="comment"># Use in an Ingress:</span>
spec:
tls:
- hosts:
- myapp.example.com
secretName: app-tls      # ← Reference TLS secret

<span class="comment"># Create generic secret from file:</span>
kubectl create secret generic ssh-key \
--from-file=id_rsa=/path/to/private-key
<span class="comment"># Key = "id_rsa", value = file contents</span></code></pre>
                            </div>
                        <div class="eq-explanation">
                            <div class="eq-exp-label">Explanation</div>
                            <p><code>kubectl create secret tls</code> validates that the cert and key are valid PEM format. The Secret type is <code>kubernetes.io/tls</code> with required keys <code>tls.crt</code> and <code>tls.key</code>. On the CKA, TLS secrets are used with Ingress TLS termination and are covered in the security domain. Use <code>--from-file</code> on <code>generic</code> secrets for arbitrary files (SSH keys, config files). The filename becomes the key unless you use <code>--from-file=custom-key=/path</code>.</p>
