                <div class="info-box note">
                    <h5>📖 Cross-Reference: Chapter 29 (etcd Backup &amp; Disaster Recovery)</h5>
                    <p>Restoring an etcd snapshot to recover from a disaster does <strong>not</strong> restore certificates — a snapshot is pure key-value data, no PKI material. If you rebuild etcd on a brand-new node (e.g. the old control-plane node is gone entirely), that new node still needs etcd's own CA (<code>etcd/ca.crt</code> + <code>ca.key</code>) copied over so it can mint a <code>server.crt</code>/<code>peer.crt</code> that the rest of the cluster already trusts — generating a FRESH etcd CA on the new node would make it unable to peer with survivors. See Chapter 29 for the full etcd DR runbook.</p>
