                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number">Q7</span>
                    <div class="eq-question">The API server won't start and you see TLS certificate errors in the kubelet logs. How do you troubleshoot?</div>
                    <details>
                        <summary>Show Answer</summary>
                            <div class="eq-answer-label">Answer</div>
                            <div class="code-block-wrapper">
                                <div class="code-block-header"><span class="code-dot red"></span><span class="code-dot yellow"></span><span class="code-dot green"></span><span class="code-lang">check kubelet logs for api server errors</span></div>
                            <pre><code class="language-bash"><span class="comment"># Step 1: Check kubelet logs for API server errors</span>
journalctl -u kubelet -l --no-pager | grep -i "tls\|cert\|x509" | tail -20
<span class="comment"># "x509: certificate has expired or is not yet valid"</span>
<span class="comment"># "tls: private key does not match public key"</span>

<span class="comment"># Step 2: Check cert expiry</span>
openssl x509 -in /etc/kubernetes/pki/apiserver.crt \
-noout -enddate -checkend 0
<span class="comment"># Certificate has expired ← Problem found!</span>

<span class="comment"># Step 3: Check cert-key match</span>
openssl x509 -in /etc/kubernetes/pki/apiserver.crt \
-noout -modulus | md5sum
openssl rsa -in /etc/kubernetes/pki/apiserver.key \
-noout -modulus | md5sum
<span class="comment"># If hashes differ → cert/key mismatch!</span>

<span class="comment"># Step 4: Check static pod manifest references correct files</span>
cat /etc/kubernetes/manifests/kube-apiserver.yaml | grep -E "cert|key"
<span class="comment">#   --tls-cert-file=/etc/kubernetes/pki/apiserver.crt</span>
<span class="comment">#   --tls-private-key-file=/etc/kubernetes/pki/apiserver.key</span>

<span class="comment"># Step 5: Fix expired certs</span>
sudo kubeadm certs renew apiserver
sudo kubeadm certs renew apiserver-kubelet-client

<span class="comment"># Step 6: Restart</span>
sudo systemctl restart kubelet

<span class="comment"># Step 7: Verify API is back</span>
kubectl get nodes</code></pre>
                            </div>
                        <div class="eq-explanation">
                            <div class="eq-exp-label">Explanation</div>
                            <p>TLS troubleshooting: check kubelet logs for x509 errors, verify cert expiry, confirm cert/key match (modulus comparison), verify manifest paths. Common causes: (1) expired certs — renew with kubeadm, (2) cert/key mismatch — regenerate, (3) wrong file paths in manifests — fix the static pod YAML. On the CKA, <code>journalctl -u kubelet</code> is your first stop when the API server is down.</p>
                        </div>
                    </details>
                </div>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number">Q8</span>
                    <div class="eq-question">What is the difference between the cluster CA certificate and component certificates?</div>
                    <details>
                        <summary>Show Answer</summary>
                            <div class="eq-answer-label">Answer</div>
                            <table>
                                <thead>
                                    <tr>
                                        <th>Certificate</th>
                                        <th>Type</th>
                                        <th>Purpose</th>
                                        <th>Validity</th>
                                    </tr>
                                </thead>
                                <tbody>
                                    <tr>
                                        <td><code>ca.crt/key</code></td>
                                        <td>Root CA</td>
                                        <td>Signs all other certs</td>
                                        <td>10 years</td>
                                    </tr>
                                    <tr>
                                        <td><code>apiserver.crt</code></td>
                                        <td>Server cert</td>
                                        <td>API server TLS</td>
                                        <td>1 year</td>
                                    </tr>
                                    <tr>
                                        <td><code>apiserver-kubelet-client</code></td>
                                        <td>Client cert</td>
                                        <td>API→kubelet auth</td>
                                        <td>1 year</td>
                                    </tr>
                                    <tr>
                                        <td><code>apiserver-etcd-client</code></td>
                                        <td>Client cert</td>
                                        <td>API→etcd auth</td>
                                        <td>1 year</td>
                                    </tr>
                                    <tr>
                                        <td><code>front-proxy-*</code></td>
                                        <td>Proxy CA+cert</td>
                                        <td>Aggregation layer</td>
                                        <td>1 year</td>
                                    </tr>
                                    <tr>
                                        <td><code>etcd/ca.crt</code></td>
                                        <td>etcd CA</td>
                                        <td>etcd internal TLS</td>
                                        <td>10 years</td>
                                    </tr>
                                </tbody>
                            </table>
                            <div class="code-block-wrapper">
                                <div class="code-block-header"><span class="code-dot red"></span><span class="code-dot yellow"></span><span class="code-dot green"></span><span class="code-lang">verify cert is signed by cluster ca</span></div>
                            <pre><code class="language-bash"><span class="comment"># Verify cert is signed by cluster CA:</span>
openssl verify -CAfile /etc/kubernetes/pki/ca.crt \
/etc/kubernetes/pki/apiserver.crt
<span class="comment"># apiserver.crt: OK</span></code></pre>
                            </div>
                        <div class="eq-explanation">
                            <div class="eq-exp-label">Explanation</div>
                            <p>The cluster CA (<code>ca.crt/ca.key</code>) is the trust root — it signs all component certs. CAs last 10 years; component certs last 1 year. There are TWO CAs: the cluster CA (for API server, kubelets) and the etcd CA (for etcd peers/clients). On the CKA, <code>openssl verify</code> checks that a cert was signed by a specific CA. Client certs authenticate components to each other (mutual TLS). If any component cert doesn't chain to the correct CA, communication fails.</p>
                        </div>
                    </details>
                </div>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number">Q9</span>
                    <div class="eq-question">How do you deny a CertificateSigningRequest and list all CSRs?</div>
                    <details>
                        <summary>Show Answer</summary>
                            <div class="eq-answer-label">Answer</div>
                            <div class="code-block-wrapper">
                                <div class="code-block-header"><span class="code-dot red"></span><span class="code-dot yellow"></span><span class="code-dot green"></span><span class="code-lang">list all csrs</span></div>
                            <pre><code class="language-bash"><span class="comment"># List all CSRs:</span>
kubectl get csr
<span class="comment"># NAME          AGE   SIGNERNAME                         REQUESTOR       CONDITION</span>
<span class="comment"># devuser-csr   2m    kubernetes.io/kube-apiserver-client admin           Approved,Issued</span>
<span class="comment"># baduser-csr   1m    kubernetes.io/kube-apiserver-client admin           Pending</span>

<span class="comment"># Deny a CSR:</span>
kubectl certificate deny baduser-csr
<span class="comment"># certificatesigningrequest.certificates.k8s.io/baduser-csr denied</span>

<span class="comment"># Delete a CSR:</span>
kubectl delete csr baduser-csr

<span class="comment"># View CSR details:</span>
kubectl get csr devuser-csr -o yaml
<span class="comment"># status:</span>
<span class="comment">#   conditions:</span>
<span class="comment">#   - type: Approved</span>
<span class="comment">#     reason: KubectlApprove</span>
<span class="comment">#     message: "This CSR was approved by kubectl certificate approve."</span>

<span class="comment"># Describe for more info:</span>
kubectl describe csr devuser-csr
<span class="comment"># Requesting User:  kubernetes-admin</span>
<span class="comment"># Signer:          kubernetes.io/kube-apiserver-client</span>
<span class="comment"># Status:          Approved,Issued</span></code></pre>
