  │            │                                                                 │
  │   ┌────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────┐                  │
  │   │        │  ALLOWED VERSION RANGES                      │                  │
  │   │        │                                              │                  │
  │   │  kubelet:         v1.28 to v1.31  (N-3 to N)         │                  │
  │   │  kube-proxy:      v1.28 to v1.31  (N-3 to N)         │                  │
  │   │  controller-mgr:  v1.30 to v1.31  (match or N-1)     │                  │
  │   │  scheduler:       v1.30 to v1.31  (match or N-1)     │                  │
  │   │  kubectl:         v1.30 to v1.32  (N-1 to N+1)       │                  │
  │   │                                                       │                  │
  │   │  ⚠️ kubelet CANNOT be newer than API server!          │                  │
  │   │  ⚠️ This is why you upgrade control plane FIRST!      │                  │
  │   └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘                  │
  │                                                                              │
  │   EXAMPLE: API server at v1.31                                               │
  │   ┌──────────┬───────────────┬──────────────┐                               │
  │   │Component │  OK Versions  │  NOT OK      │                               │
  │   ├──────────┼───────────────┼──────────────┤                               │
  │   │kubelet   │ 1.28-1.31     │ 1.27, 1.32   │                               │
  │   │kubectl   │ 1.30,1.31,1.32│ 1.29         │                               │
  │   │scheduler │ 1.30, 1.31    │ 1.29, 1.32   │                               │
  │   └──────────┴───────────────┴──────────────┘                               │
  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
</pre>
</div>
                </div>

                <div class="info-box warning">
                    <h5>⚠️ Why Control Plane First?</h5>
                    <p>kubelet can be <strong>up to three minor versions behind</strong> the API server (N-3, widened from N-2 back in Kubernetes 1.25 — clusters older than that only allowed N-2), but <strong>never ahead</strong> — that "never ahead" rule is absolute and has nothing to do with the N-3 window. If you upgrade a worker first, its kubelet becomes v1.31 while the API server is still v1.30 — the kubelet is now <em>ahead</em> of the API server, which violates the skew policy outright and causes unpredictable behavior (the kubelet may report status the API server's older code doesn't expect). Always: <strong>control plane → workers</strong>.</p>
                </div>
            </section>

