                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number">Q2</span>
                    <div class="eq-question">Upgrade a worker node from 1.30.0 to 1.31.0. Include draining and uncordoning.</div>
                    <details>
                        <summary>Show Answer</summary>
                            <div class="eq-answer-label">Answer</div>
                            <div class="code-block-wrapper">
                                <div class="code-block-header"><span class="code-dot red"></span><span class="code-dot yellow"></span><span class="code-dot green"></span><span class="code-lang">from control plane</span></div>
                            <pre><code class="language-bash"><span class="comment"># FROM CONTROL PLANE:</span>
<span class="comment"># Step 1: Drain the worker node</span>
kubectl drain worker-1 --ignore-daemonsets --delete-emptydir-data
<span class="comment"># node/worker-1 cordoned</span>
<span class="comment"># evicting pod default/web-app-xxxxx</span>
<span class="comment"># pod/web-app-xxxxx evicted</span>

<span class="comment"># ON WORKER NODE (ssh worker-1):</span>
<span class="comment"># Step 2: Upgrade kubeadm</span>
sudo apt-get update
sudo apt-get install -y --allow-change-held-packages \
kubeadm=1.31.0-1.1
sudo apt-mark hold kubeadm

<span class="comment"># Step 3: Upgrade node config</span>
sudo kubeadm upgrade node
<span class="comment"># [upgrade] Successfully upgraded node config</span>

<span class="comment"># Step 4: Upgrade kubelet and kubectl</span>
sudo apt-get install -y --allow-change-held-packages \
kubelet=1.31.0-1.1 kubectl=1.31.0-1.1
sudo apt-mark hold kubelet kubectl

<span class="comment"># Step 5: Restart kubelet</span>
sudo systemctl daemon-reload
sudo systemctl restart kubelet

<span class="comment"># BACK ON CONTROL PLANE:</span>
<span class="comment"># Step 6: Uncordon the worker</span>
kubectl uncordon worker-1
<span class="comment"># node/worker-1 uncordoned</span>

<span class="comment"># Step 7: Verify</span>
kubectl get nodes
<span class="comment"># NAME           STATUS   ROLES          VERSION</span>
<span class="comment"># controlplane   Ready    control-plane  v1.31.0</span>
<span class="comment"># worker-1       Ready    &lt;none&gt;         v1.31.0</span></code></pre>
                            </div>
                        <div class="eq-explanation">
                            <div class="eq-exp-label">Explanation</div>
                            <p>Worker upgrade: drain (from control plane) → SSH to worker → upgrade kubeadm → <code>kubeadm upgrade node</code> (NOT <code>apply</code>) → upgrade kubelet/kubectl → restart → uncordon (from control plane). Key differences from control plane: workers use <code>kubeadm upgrade node</code> (not <code>apply</code>), and you MUST drain before upgrading. Forgetting to uncordon is a common CKA mistake — the node stays <code>SchedulingDisabled</code>.</p>
                        </div>
                    </details>
                </div>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number">Q3</span>
                    <div class="eq-question">What is the Kubernetes version skew policy? Which component version relationships must be maintained?</div>
                    <details>
                        <summary>Show Answer</summary>
                            <div class="eq-answer-label">Answer</div>
                            <table>
                                <thead>
                                    <tr>
                                        <th>Component</th>
                                        <th>Relative to API Server</th>
                                        <th>Example (API=1.31)</th>
                                    </tr>
                                </thead>
                                <tbody>
                                    <tr>
                                        <td>kubelet</td>
                                        <td>Up to 3 minor behind</td>
                                        <td>1.28 – 1.31</td>
                                    </tr>
                                    <tr>
                                        <td>kube-proxy</td>
                                        <td>Same or 3 minor behind</td>
                                        <td>1.28 – 1.31</td>
                                    </tr>
                                    <tr>
                                        <td>kubectl</td>
                                        <td>±1 minor version</td>
                                        <td>1.30 – 1.32</td>
                                    </tr>
                                    <tr>
                                        <td>controller-manager</td>
                                        <td>Same minor version, or up to 1 behind</td>
                                        <td>1.30 – 1.31</td>
                                    </tr>
                                    <tr>
                                        <td>scheduler</td>
                                        <td>Same minor version, or up to 1 behind</td>
                                        <td>1.30 – 1.31</td>
                                    </tr>
                                </tbody>
                            </table>
                            <div class="code-block-wrapper">
                                <div class="code-block-header"><span class="code-dot red"></span><span class="code-dot yellow"></span><span class="code-dot green"></span><span class="code-lang">key rules</span></div>
                            <pre><code class="language-bash"><span class="comment"># Key rules:</span>
<span class="comment"># 1. NEVER skip minor versions (1.30→1.32 = INVALID)</span>
<span class="comment"># 2. Upgrade control plane BEFORE workers</span>
<span class="comment"># 3. API server is always the newest component</span>

<span class="comment"># Check current versions:</span>
kubectl get nodes -o wide
kubectl version --short</code></pre>
                            </div>
                        <div class="eq-explanation">
                            <div class="eq-exp-label">Explanation</div>
                            <p>The version skew policy ensures component compatibility. Key rules: kubelet can lag up to 3 minor versions behind the API server, kubectl is ±1, and control plane components must match. You cannot skip minor versions during upgrades (must upgrade sequentially). On the CKA, they may show you a cluster with mixed versions and ask if it's valid. The API server is always the "baseline" — everything is measured relative to it.</p>
                        </div>
                    </details>
