<span class="comment"># Now check again:</span>
apt-cache madison kubeadm
<span class="comment"># kubeadm | 1.31.0-1.1 | ... ← Now visible!</span>

<span class="comment"># Continue with normal upgrade:</span>
sudo apt-get install -y kubeadm=1.31.0-1.1</code></pre>
                            </div>
                        <div class="eq-explanation">
                            <div class="eq-exp-label">Explanation</div>
                            <p>Since the community package repositories at <code>pkgs.k8s.io</code> replaced the old <code>apt.kubernetes.io</code>/<code>yum.kubernetes.io</code> repos (mandatory for every Kubernetes release since September 2023), packages are hosted in version-specific repositories. Each minor version (1.30, 1.31) has its own repo URL. If <code>madison</code> doesn't show the target version, the repo needs updating. On the CKA, the exam environment may already have the correct repo configured, but if not, you need to know how to update it. Always <code>apt-get update</code> after changing the repo.</p>
                        </div>
                    </details>
                </div>
