            <span class="ch-jump" id="ch28-drill"></span>
            <div class="cka-practice-drill">
                <h4>🔬 Practice Drill 28.1 — Upgrade the Control Plane</h4>
                <div class="drill-timer">⏱️ Target Time: 8 minutes</div>
                <div class="drill-scenario">
                    <h5>Scenario</h5>
                    <p>Your cluster is running Kubernetes v1.30.0. You need to upgrade the <strong>control plane node</strong> named <code>controlplane</code> to v1.31.0. Complete the full upgrade process.</p>
                    <ol>
                        <li>Upgrade kubeadm to 1.31.0-1.1 on the control plane</li>
                        <li>Run the upgrade plan and apply the upgrade</li>
                        <li>Drain the control plane node</li>
                        <li>Upgrade kubelet and kubectl to 1.31.0-1.1</li>
                        <li>Restart kubelet and uncordon the node</li>
                        <li>Verify the control plane shows v1.31.0</li>
                    </ol>
                </div>
                <div class="drill-hint">
                    <strong>Hint:</strong> Remember the order — kubeadm first, then plan/apply, then drain, then kubelet/kubectl. Don't forget <code>apt-mark hold</code> after each install and <code>daemon-reload</code> before restart.
                </div>
                <div class="drill-solution">
                    <details>
                        <summary>View Solution</summary>
                        <pre><code class="language-bash"><span class="comment"># On controlplane node:</span>

<span class="comment"># 1. Upgrade kubeadm</span>
apt-mark unhold kubeadm
apt-get update && apt-get install -y kubeadm=1.31.0-1.1
apt-mark hold kubeadm

<span class="comment"># 2. Plan and apply</span>
kubeadm upgrade plan
kubeadm upgrade apply v1.31.0

<span class="comment"># 3. Drain</span>
kubectl drain controlplane --ignore-daemonsets

<span class="comment"># 4. Upgrade kubelet and kubectl</span>
apt-mark unhold kubelet kubectl
