            <div class="cka-practice-drill">
                <h4>🔬 Practice Drill 28.4 — Diagnose a Version Skew</h4>
                <div class="drill-timer">⏱️ Target Time: 4 minutes</div>
                <div class="drill-scenario">
                    <h5>Scenario</h5>
                    <p><code>kubectl get nodes -o wide</code> shows: <code>controlplane v1.31.0</code>, <code>worker01 v1.28.0</code>, <code>worker02 v1.27.2</code>. A teammate says "worker02 is clearly broken, it's 4 versions behind!" Determine whether they're right, and what (if anything) you need to fix.</p>
                    <ol>
                        <li>Work out how many minor versions behind the API server each worker is</li>
                        <li>Decide which node(s), if any, violate the version skew policy</li>
                        <li>State the exact upgrade command(s) needed to bring the cluster into compliance</li>
                    </ol>
                </div>
                <div class="drill-hint">
                    <strong>Hint:</strong> The current policy (since Kubernetes 1.25) allows kubelet to be up to <strong>3</strong> minor versions behind the API server — not 1. Count the actual minor-version gap for each node before concluding anything is broken.
                </div>
                <div class="drill-solution">
                    <details>
                        <summary>View Solution</summary>
                        <pre><code class="language-bash"><span class="comment"># API server: v1.31 (the baseline)</span>
<span class="comment"># worker01:   v1.28  →  1.31 - 1.28 = 3 minor versions behind  →  ✅ WITHIN policy (N-3 is the max allowed)</span>
<span class="comment"># worker02:   v1.27  →  1.31 - 1.27 = 4 minor versions behind  →  ❌ VIOLATES policy (only N-3 allowed, this is N-4)</span>

<span class="comment"># Your teammate was half right: worker01 is fine (exactly at the N-3 limit).</span>
<span class="comment"># worker02 IS actually out of policy — it needs to be upgraded, but NOT directly to 1.31</span>
<span class="comment"># (kubeadm forbids skipping minor versions during the upgrade itself).</span>

<span class="comment"># Fix worker02 — upgrade one minor version at a time until compliant:</span>
<span class="comment"># Step 1: drain from control plane</span>
kubectl drain worker02 --ignore-daemonsets --delete-emptydir-data

<span class="comment"># Step 2: SSH to worker02, upgrade to 1.28 first (kubeadm won't let you skip to 1.31 in one hop)</span>
ssh worker02
apt-mark unhold kubeadm && apt-get update && apt-get install -y kubeadm=1.28.0-1.1 && apt-mark hold kubeadm
kubeadm upgrade node
apt-mark unhold kubelet kubectl && apt-get install -y kubelet=1.28.0-1.1 kubectl=1.28.0-1.1 && apt-mark hold kubelet kubectl
systemctl daemon-reload && systemctl restart kubelet
exit

<span class="comment"># Step 3: back on control plane, uncordon and verify</span>
kubectl uncordon worker02
kubectl get nodes
<span class="comment"># worker02 now v1.28.0 — 3 minor behind v1.31 — ✅ compliant</span>
<span class="comment"># (Repeat the same one-minor-at-a-time climb again later if you want worker02 fully caught up to v1.31.)</span></code></pre>
                    </details>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="cka-practice-drill">
                <h4>🔬 Practice Drill 28.5 — Full 3-Node HA Cluster Upgrade</h4>
