            <!-- Section 29.3 — etcd Restore                                -->
            <!-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
            <!-- ─────────── §29.3 ─────────── -->
            <section class="section-block" id="s29-3">                    <h3 class="section-h">29.3 etcd Restore</h3>
                    <span class="badge badge-exam">🎯 CKA EXAM TOPIC</span>

                <p>Restoring from a snapshot is a <strong>multi-step process</strong>. You restore to a new data directory, then update the etcd static pod manifest to point to it. The kubelet detects the manifest change and restarts etcd with the restored data.</p>

                <div class="card-grid cols-2">
                    <div class="scenario-box positive">
                        <h5>💾 Backup Command</h5>
                        <p><code>ETCDCTL_API=3 etcdctl snapshot save /opt/backup.db</code></p>
                        <ul>
                            <li>Needs <strong>4 TLS flags</strong> (endpoints, cacert, cert, key)</li>
                            <li>Creates a single snapshot file</li>
                            <li>Non-disruptive (cluster keeps running)</li>
                            <li>No manifest changes needed</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    <div class="scenario-box">
                        <h5>🔄 Restore Command</h5>
