            <section class="section-block" id="s29-5">                    <h3 class="section-h">29.5 Beyond etcd — Velero</h3>

                <p>Everything in §29.1-29.4 protects the cluster's <strong>desired-state objects</strong> — the Deployment spec, the Secret, the PVC. None of it protects the <strong>bytes</strong> inside easypj's PostgreSQL PersistentVolume. To get a full disaster-recovery story for easypj — one that survives losing a namespace, a node, or an entire cluster — you need a tool built for that job: <strong>Velero</strong>.</p>

