                <div class="info-box tip">
                    <h5>💡 Insight — Velero Is Also Your Migration Tool</h5>
                    <p>Because a Velero backup lives in object storage (S3, GCS, Azure Blob) independent of any single cluster, <code>velero backup create easypj-daily</code> on cluster A followed by <code>velero restore create --from-backup easypj-daily</code> on cluster B moves easypj's namespace AND its PostgreSQL data to a brand-new cluster — no manual YAML re-authoring, no manual database dump/restore. A GitOps repository (re-applying all manifests) is itself a form of DR for the API <em>objects</em>, but it still needs pairing with a volume-level backup for the <em>data</em> — GitOps alone won't bring back a single row of postgres.</p>
