            <section class="section-block" id="s30-1">                    <h3 class="section-h">30.1 Draining Nodes — Safe Pod Eviction</h3>
                    <span class="badge badge-exam">🎯 CKA EXAM TOPIC</span>

                <p>Before maintenance, you must safely move all pods off a node. Kubernetes provides three commands for this: <code>drain</code>, <code>cordon</code>, and <code>uncordon</code>. Understanding when to use each is critical.</p>

                <div class="card-grid cols-2">
                    <div class="info-card highlight">
                        <div class="card-icon-lg">🚿</div>
                        <h5>kubectl drain</h5>
                        <p>Cordons the node <strong>AND</strong> evicts all pods (except DaemonSets). Use before maintenance. Almost always needs <code>--ignore-daemonsets</code>.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="info-card">
                        <div class="card-icon-lg">🚧</div>
                        <h5>kubectl cordon</h5>
                        <p>Marks node as <strong>SchedulingDisabled</strong> — no new pods scheduled, but existing pods <strong>keep running</strong>. Use to gradually move workloads.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="info-card">
                        <div class="card-icon-lg">✅</div>
                        <h5>kubectl uncordon</h5>
                        <p>Removes the SchedulingDisabled mark — node accepts new pods again. <strong>Always run after maintenance</strong> or pods won't come back.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="info-card">
                        <div class="card-icon-lg">🛡️</div>
                        <h5>PodDisruptionBudget</h5>
                        <p>Controls <strong>how many pods can be evicted at once</strong>. Drain respects PDBs — if evicting would violate <code>minAvailable</code>, drain blocks until safe.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Drain vs Cordon vs Uncordon Comparison -->
                <div class="comparison-table">
                    <h4>📊 drain vs cordon vs uncordon</h4>
                    <table>
                        <thead>
                            <tr>
                                <th>Command</th>
                                <th>Marks Unschedulable?</th>
