                <!-- HA Control-Plane Draining — production nuance beyond a single-node worker drain -->
                <p>Everything above assumes you're draining a <strong>worker</strong> node. Draining a <strong>control-plane</strong> node in a highly-available (HA) cluster follows the same <code>cordon → drain → patch → uncordon</code> shape, but carries a risk that doesn't exist on workers: draining the wrong control-plane node at the wrong time can take down the API server or break etcd's <strong>raft quorum</strong> for the whole cluster, not just one app.</p>

