                <div class="info-box danger">
                    <h5>🚨 Production Rule: Never Start Node Maintenance Against a Deployment Mid-Rollout</h5>
                    <p>Before draining any node, check <code>kubectl rollout status deployment/&lt;name&gt; -n &lt;namespace&gt;</code> for every Deployment with pods on that node. If it reports anything other than <code>successfully rolled out</code>, either wait for the rollout to finish (or roll it back with <code>kubectl rollout undo</code>) before draining — don't stack a planned maintenance drain on top of an in-progress rollout that's already consuming the same PDB's headroom. This is the same underlying lesson as the HA control-plane rule above: when two operations draw from one shared budget, run them <strong>sequentially</strong>, never concurrently.</p>
