                    <tbody>
                        <tr><td><a href="#s31-1"><strong>31.1</strong> Pod Lifecycle &amp; Status Codes</a></td><td>What do these states/codes mean?</td><td>Phase = triage colour; container State + exit code = the real diagnosis.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><a href="#s31-2"><strong>31.2</strong> The Debugging Toolkit</a></td><td>What order do I investigate in?</td><td>status → describe(Events) → logs --previous → exec → events. Always.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><a href="#s31-3"><strong>31.3</strong> Essential Debug Commands</a></td><td>What's the exact syntax?</td><td>One memorized command per step, plus <code>kubectl debug</code> for distroless.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><a href="#s31-4"><strong>31.4</strong> Debugging easypj — Common Scenarios</a></td><td>How does this play out for real?</td><td>CrashLoop (DB refused), Pending (memory), 502 (bind address), and more.</td></tr>
                    </tbody>
