                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="info-box warning">
                    <h5>⚠️ Don't Confuse This With CrashLoopBackOff</h5>
                    <p>CreateContainerConfigError is a <strong>pre-flight</strong> failure — the kubelet refuses to even create the container because a referenced ConfigMap/Secret/key is missing, so <code>kubectl logs</code> (with or without <code>--previous</code>) will always return nothing ("previous terminated container not found" or empty). Don't waste exam time re-running <code>logs</code> on a loop here — go straight to <code>describe</code> Events, which names the missing object, and create it. This is also why <code>RESTARTS</code> stays at <code>0</code>: the container has never actually started, so there is nothing to restart.</p>
                </div>
