            <div class="uth-callout"><strong>🔑 Always ask "one layer down."</strong> When a Pod symptom (Ch 31) doesn't have an obvious Pod-level cause (bad image, bad probe, resource limit), the next question is never "what's wrong with the Pod" again — it's "what's wrong with the NODE this Pod landed on" (Ch 32), checked with the instruments from Ch 33. A CrashLoopBackOff that survives a <code>kubectl delete pod</code> (it just crashes again on the new Pod too) is the tell that the real cause is environmental, not the container image.</div>
