<span class="comment"># DaemonSet recreates them</span>

<span class="comment"># Fix 3: Check node network</span>
ssh worker-1
ip link show  <span class="comment"># Network interfaces</span>
ip route     <span class="comment"># Routing table</span>

<span class="comment"># Verify: Pods should move from ContainerCreating to Running</span>
kubectl get pods -w</code></pre>
                            </div>
                        <div class="eq-explanation">
                            <div class="eq-exp-label">Explanation</div>
                            <p>CNI provides pod networking. Without CNI, pods can't get IP addresses and stay in ContainerCreating. On the CKA: check <code>/etc/cni/net.d/</code> for config files and <code>/opt/cni/bin/</code> for binaries. If no CNI is installed, you need to apply the CNI plugin manifest. CNI plugins run as DaemonSets in <code>kube-system</code>. Common exam question: "pods stuck in ContainerCreating on a new node" = CNI not configured.</p>
