                <div class="info-box warning">
                    <h5>⚠️ Lab Fix — The <code>--kubelet-insecure-tls</code> Flag</h5>
                    <p>kubelets in kubeadm/kind/minikube clusters use <strong>self-signed certificates</strong>, so metrics-server's scrape fails TLS verification and stays "unavailable" forever unless you tell it to skip verification. This is one of the most common CKA lab gotchas.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="code-block-wrapper">
                    <div class="code-block-header">
                        <span class="code-dot red"></span>
                        <span class="code-dot yellow"></span>
                        <span class="code-dot green"></span>
                        <span class="code-lang">metrics-server-lab-patch.yaml</span>
                    </div>
<pre><code class="language-yaml"><span class="comment"># The full Deployment shape — showing WHERE the flag goes:</span>
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: metrics-server
  namespace: kube-system
spec:
  template:
    spec:
      containers:
        - name: metrics-server
          args:
            - --cert-dir=/tmp
            - --secure-port=10250
            - --kubelet-preferred-address-types=InternalIP,Hostname,ExternalIP
            - --kubelet-use-node-status-port
            - --metric-resolution=15s
            - --kubelet-insecure-tls          <span class="comment"># ← the lab-critical flag</span>

<span class="comment"># Quick imperative one-liner instead of editing the file:</span>
<span class="comment"># kubectl patch deployment metrics-server -n kube-system --type=json \</span>
<span class="comment">#   -p='[{"op":"add","path":"/spec/template/spec/containers/0/args/-",</span>
<span class="comment">#         "value":"--kubelet-insecure-tls"}]'</span></code></pre>
                </div>

                <h4>🩺 Troubleshooting <code>kubectl top</code> Errors</h4>
                <div class="comparison-table">
                    <table>
                        <thead>
                            <tr><th>#</th><th>Check</th><th>Command</th></tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr><td>1</td><td>Is metrics-server even installed?</td><td><code>kubectl get deploy -n kube-system metrics-server</code></td></tr>
                            <tr><td>2</td><td>Is its Pod Ready?</td><td><code>kubectl get pods -n kube-system | grep metrics</code></td></tr>
                            <tr><td>3</td><td>Is the APIService healthy?</td><td><code>kubectl get apiservice v1beta1.metrics.k8s.io</code></td></tr>
                            <tr><td>4</td><td>Do logs show TLS errors?</td><td><code>kubectl logs -n kube-system deploy/metrics-server</code> → add <code>--kubelet-insecure-tls</code></td></tr>
                            <tr><td>5</td><td>Just installed?</td><td>Wait one scrape interval (~15-30s), then retry — don't assume it's broken</td></tr>
                        </tbody>
