┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  HOW kubectl top GETS A NUMBER — THREE HOPS                                  │
│                                                                              │
│  Linux kernel cgroups (per-container CPU/memory accounting)                  │
│       │                                                                     │
│       ▼                                                                     │
│  🤖 cAdvisor (built into every kubelet, no separate install)                 │
│       │  exposes it on the kubelet's secure port (10250) via                │
│       │  /metrics/resource (current metrics-server default) — older         │
│       │  metrics-server builds instead used /stats/summary (Summary API)    │
│       ▼                                                                     │
│  📊 metrics-server (Deployment in kube-system)                              │
│       │  scrapes EVERY kubelet's resource endpoint every --metric-resolution│
│       │  (default 15s) and aggregates into an in-MEMORY snapshot            │
│       ▼                                                                     │
│  🌐 metrics.k8s.io API  (registered via the API aggregation layer,           │
│       │                  NOT stored in etcd — this is deliberate!)          │
│       ▼                                                                     │
