'NAME:.metadata.name,CPU_REQ:.spec.containers[0].resources.requests.cpu,CPU_LIM:.spec.containers[0].resources.limits.cpu,MEM_REQ:.spec.containers[0].resources.requests.memory,MEM_LIM:.spec.containers[0].resources.limits.memory'
<span class="comment"># NAME       CPU_REQ  CPU_LIM  MEM_REQ  MEM_LIM</span>
<span class="comment"># web-pod    100m     500m     128Mi    512Mi</span>
<span class="comment"># api-pod    250m     1        256Mi    1Gi</span>

<span class="comment"># Node capacity:</span>
kubectl describe node worker-1 | grep -A5 "Capacity"
<span class="comment"># Capacity:</span>
<span class="comment">#   cpu:     4</span>
<span class="comment">#   memory:  8Gi</span>

<span class="comment"># Node allocatable (after system reservations):</span>
kubectl describe node worker-1 | grep -A5 "Allocatable"
<span class="comment"># Allocatable:</span>
<span class="comment">#   cpu:     3800m</span>
<span class="comment">#   memory:  7500Mi</span>

<span class="comment"># What's allocated on the node:</span>
kubectl describe node worker-1 | grep -A10 "Allocated"
<span class="comment"># Allocated resources:</span>
<span class="comment">#   CPU Requests  (Limits)    Memory Requests  (Limits)</span>
<span class="comment">#   1500m (39%)   3000m (78%) 2Gi (26%)        4Gi (53%)</span>

<span class="comment"># Available = Allocatable - Allocated</span>
<span class="comment"># CPU: 3800m - 1500m = 2300m free for scheduling</span>
<span class="comment"># Memory: 7500Mi - 2048Mi = 5452Mi free</span>

<span class="comment"># Actual usage vs requests (are pods using what they asked for?):</span>
kubectl top pods
<span class="comment"># Compare kubectl top (actual) vs requests (reserved)</span></code></pre>
                            </div>
                        <div class="eq-explanation">
                            <div class="eq-exp-label">Explanation</div>
                            <p>Three levels: Capacity (total), Allocatable (after reservations), Allocated (sum of requests). On the CKA: scheduling uses requests (not limits or actual usage). If a pod requests 500m CPU and the node only has 300m allocatable, it won't schedule. <code>kubectl describe node</code> shows all three levels. <code>kubectl top</code> shows actual real-time usage. Common pitfall: pods requesting more than they use wastes resources.</p>
                        </div>
                    </details>
                </div>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
