                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- ── Scenario 11: Scheduler Down ── -->
                <h4>Scenario 11: Scheduler Down — Pods Stay Pending Forever</h4>
                <div class="info-box warning">
                    <h5>⚠️ Problem</h5>
                    <p>Every new <code>easypj</code> pod sticks at <code>Pending</code> — and <code>kubectl describe</code> shows <strong>no scheduling Events at all</strong>. Nothing is even trying to place them, which is a very different symptom than Scenario 2's "FailedScheduling" Events.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="diagram-container">
                    <h4>🔴 Scheduler Down — Static Pod Diagnosis</h4>
                    <div class="diagram-box">
                    <pre>
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  1. IDENTIFY:                                                           │
│     $ kubectl get pods -n easypj                                        │
│     easypj-web-yyyy   0/1   Pending   0   10m                           │
│     $ kubectl describe pod easypj-web-yyyy -n easypj                    │
│     Events:  &lt;none&gt;   ◄── NOTHING is even trying to schedule this!     │
│     (compare to Scenario 2, which showed a FailedScheduling Event)      │
│                                                                         │
│  2. GATHER — Check the scheduler static pod:                            │
│     $ kubectl get pods -n kube-system | grep scheduler                  │
│     kube-scheduler-master   0/1   CrashLoopBackOff   5   ◄── found it!  │
│     (or the pod is MISSING from the list entirely)                     │
│                                                                         │
│  3. ANALYZE — Inspect its manifest &amp; runtime on the master:            │
│     $ ls /etc/kubernetes/manifests/kube-scheduler.yaml                  │
│     $ crictl ps -a | grep scheduler                                     │
│     $ crictl logs &lt;scheduler-container-id&gt;                             │
│     → Error: unknown flag --leader-elect-lease-durationn   ◄── typo!    │
│                                                                         │
│  4. FIX — Correct the static-pod manifest:                              │
│     $ vi /etc/kubernetes/manifests/kube-scheduler.yaml                  │
│     → fix the flag typo, bad path, or wrong image tag                   │
│     (kubelet watches this directory — save = auto-restart, no apply!)   │
│                                                                         │
│  5. VERIFY:                                                             │
│     $ kubectl get pods -n kube-system | grep scheduler                  │
│     kube-scheduler-master   1/1   Running   ← ✅ Fixed!                │
│     $ kubectl get pods -n easypj -w                                     │
│     easypj-web-yyyy   1/1   Running   ← ✅ It schedules now!           │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                    </pre>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="cka-gotcha">
                    <h5>⚠️ Don't confuse this with Scenario 2</h5>
                    <p>Scenario 2 (Pod Pending) has a <code>FailedScheduling</code> Event — the scheduler is running and actively rejecting the pod (taint/resources/affinity). Scenario 11 has <strong>zero scheduling Events</strong> — the scheduler itself isn't running to make a decision at all. "No Events" is the tell that points you at the control plane, not the pod spec.</p>
                </div>

                <!-- ── Scenario 12: ImagePullBackOff ── -->
                <h4>Scenario 12: ImagePullBackOff</h4>
                <div class="info-box warning">
                    <h5>⚠️ Problem</h5>
                    <p><code>easypj-web</code> is stuck pulling its image and never reaches <code>Running</code>.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="diagram-container">
                    <h4>🟡 ImagePullBackOff — Three Root Causes</h4>
                    <div class="diagram-box">
                    <pre>
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  1. IDENTIFY:                                                           │
│     $ kubectl get pods -n easypj                                        │
│     easypj-web-zzzz   0/1   ImagePullBackOff   0   3m                   │
│                                                                         │
│  2. GATHER — Read the exact pull error in Events:                       │
│     $ kubectl describe pod easypj-web-zzzz -n easypj                    │
│     Events:                                                             │
│       Failed to pull image "easypj/jobpost:v2.1": rpc error: ...        │
│                                                                         │
│  3. ANALYZE — Match the message to one of three causes:                │
│  ┌─────────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────┐   │
│  │ Events Message                  │ Root Cause                    │   │
│  ├─────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┤   │
│  │ "not found" / "manifest unknown"│ Wrong image name or tag (typo)│   │
│  │ "unauthorized" / "pull denied"  │ Private registry, no pull secret│  │
│  │ "no such host" / timeout        │ Registry unreachable / DNS /  │   │
│  │                                  │ air-gapped node               │   │
│  └─────────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────┘   │
│                                                                         │
│  4. FIX:                                                                │
│     a) Wrong tag — correct the image reference:                        │
│        $ kubectl set image deploy/easypj-web web=easypj/jobpost:v2.0.1 │
│     b) Private registry — create &amp; attach a pull secret:               │
│        $ kubectl create secret docker-registry regcred \                │
│            --docker-server=registry.easypj.io \                        │
│            --docker-username=ci --docker-password=$TOKEN \              │
│            -n easypj                                                   │
│        $ kubectl patch sa default -n easypj \                          │
│            -p '{"imagePullSecrets":[{"name":"regcred"}]}'              │
│                                                                         │
│  5. VERIFY:                                                             │
│     $ kubectl get pods -n easypj                                        │
│     easypj-web-zzzz   1/1   Running   ← ✅ Image pulled!               │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
