│  /etc/kubernetes/pki/          → Cluster certificates                       │
│  /var/lib/kubelet/config.yaml  → kubelet configuration                      │
│  /var/log/containers/          → Container log files on node                │
│  /etc/cni/net.d/               → CNI plugin configuration                  │
│  /var/lib/etcd/                → etcd data directory                        │
│  ~/.kube/config                → kubectl configuration (kubeconfig)         │
│                                                                              │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                    </pre>
                    </div>
                </div>

                

                <div class="scenario-box">
                    <div class="scenario-header">
                        <span class="scenario-icon">🔥</span>
                        <h4>Multi-Issue Scenario: "Application Not Reachable"</h4>
                        <span class="badge badge-advanced">ADVANCED</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="scenario-content">
                        <p><strong>Situation:</strong> A 3-tier app (frontend → backend → database) reports "Connection refused" from outside the cluster. Multiple things are broken.</p>
                        <div class="scenario-steps">
                            <div class="scenario-step">
                                <span class="step-label">Layer 1 — Infrastructure</span>
                                <p>Run <code>kubectl get nodes</code>. Worker node is <strong>NotReady</strong>. SSH in, find kubelet stopped → <code>systemctl start kubelet</code>. Node recovers. Pods reschedule.</p>
                            </div>
                            <div class="scenario-step">
                                <span class="step-label">Layer 2 — Workload</span>
                                <p>Backend pod is <strong>CrashLoopBackOff</strong>. <code>kubectl logs backend --previous</code> shows missing <code>DB_HOST</code> env var. Fix: add <code>envFrom</code> referencing the ConfigMap. Pod starts.</p>
                            </div>
                            <div class="scenario-step">
                                <span class="step-label">Layer 3 — Networking</span>
