            <div class="cka-practice-drill">
                    <h4>🔬 Practice Drill 34.1 — Time Yourself on All 12 Scenarios</h4>
                    <div class="drill-timer">⏱️ Target Time: 60 minutes (5 min × 12 scenarios)</div>
                    <div class="drill-scenario">
                        <h5>Scenario</h5>
                        <p>Set up a practice cluster (kubeadm or kind). Intentionally break it in each of these 12 ways, then fix it. On the CKA exam, speed matters — solve each scenario in under 5 minutes.</p>
                        <ol>
                            <li>Stop kubelet on a worker node → diagnose and fix NotReady</li>
                            <li>Set impossible resource requests → fix Pending pod</li>
                            <li>Mismatch service selector → fix endpoints</li>
                            <li>Remove required env var → fix CrashLoopBackOff</li>
                            <li>Break CoreDNS config → fix DNS resolution</li>
                            <li>Corrupt etcd data → restore from snapshot</li>
                            <li>Let certs expire (kubeadm certs) → renew and recover</li>
                            <li>Apply overly restrictive NetworkPolicy → fix traffic flow</li>
                            <li>Create PVC with wrong StorageClass → fix binding</li>
                            <li>Delete kubeconfig → recreate from admin.conf</li>
                            <li>Break the kube-scheduler static-pod manifest → fix pods stuck Pending with zero Events</li>
                            <li>Reference a mistyped image tag → fix ImagePullBackOff</li>
                        </ol>
                    </div>
                    <div class="drill-hint">
                        <strong>Hint:</strong> Every one of these maps to a row in this chapter's "Symptom → First Response Quick-Reference" table above — if you get stuck, that's the fastest way back on track.
                    </div>
                    <div class="drill-solution">
                        <details>
                            <summary>View Solution</summary>
                            <pre><code class="language-bash"><span class="comment"># 1. NotReady worker — kubelet stopped</span>
ssh worker "sudo systemctl start kubelet"

<span class="comment"># 2. Pending pod — impossible resource request</span>
kubectl edit pod &lt;name&gt;   <span class="comment"># lower requests.memory/cpu to fit a real node, or delete+recreate</span>

<span class="comment"># 3. No endpoints — selector mismatch</span>
kubectl get svc &lt;name&gt; -o yaml   <span class="comment"># compare spec.selector against the pod's actual labels, fix one side</span>

<span class="comment"># 4. CrashLoopBackOff — missing env var</span>
kubectl logs &lt;pod&gt; --previous   <span class="comment"># confirms which var; kubectl edit deploy to add it back</span>

<span class="comment"># 5. Broken DNS — CoreDNS config</span>
kubectl edit cm coredns -n kube-system   <span class="comment"># fix the Corefile, then: kubectl rollout restart deploy coredns -n kube-system</span>

<span class="comment"># 6. Corrupt etcd — restore from snapshot</span>
ETCDCTL_API=3 etcdctl snapshot restore /opt/backup.db --data-dir=/var/lib/etcd-restored
<span class="comment"># repoint etcd.yaml's --data-dir at the restored directory</span>

<span class="comment"># 7. Expired certs — renew</span>
kubeadm certs renew all
sudo systemctl restart kubelet

<span class="comment"># 8. NetworkPolicy blocking traffic</span>
kubectl describe netpol &lt;name&gt;   <span class="comment"># check podSelector + ingress rules, loosen the offending rule</span>

<span class="comment"># 9. PVC stuck — wrong StorageClass</span>
kubectl get pvc &lt;name&gt; -o yaml   <span class="comment"># fix storageClassName to match an existing StorageClass, or create the missing one</span>

<span class="comment"># 10. Deleted kubeconfig — recreate</span>
sudo cp /etc/kubernetes/admin.conf ~/.kube/config
sudo chown $(id -u):$(id -g) ~/.kube/config

<span class="comment"># 11. Scheduler down — broken static-pod manifest (zero scheduling Events is the tell)</span>
sudo vi /etc/kubernetes/manifests/kube-scheduler.yaml   <span class="comment"># fix the flag/path/image typo; kubelet auto-restarts it</span>
kubectl -n kube-system get pods | grep scheduler         <span class="comment"># confirm 1/1 Running</span>

<span class="comment"># 12. ImagePullBackOff — bad tag or missing pull secret</span>
kubectl describe pod &lt;name&gt;   <span class="comment"># read the exact Events message: "not found" vs "unauthorized" vs "no such host"</span>
kubectl set image deploy/easypj-web web=easypj/jobpost:v2.0.1   <span class="comment"># OR create+attach an imagePullSecret</span></code></pre>
                        </details>
                    </div>
