<span class="comment"># easypj-web pods reschedule onto worker02 once it's Ready again</span>
<span class="comment"># The CrashLoopBackOff was actually pods stuck retry-scheduling on a dying node —</span>
<span class="comment"># once rescheduled onto a healthy node they start clean</span>

kubectl get endpoints easypj-svc -n easypj
<span class="comment"># populated now too — there were simply no Ready pods to be an endpoint</span>

<span class="comment"># Step 3 — VERIFY all three symptoms are gone</span>
kubectl get nodes            <span class="comment"># All Ready</span>
kubectl get pods -n easypj   <span class="comment"># All Running, 0 recent restarts</span>
kubectl get endpoints -n easypj  <span class="comment"># Populated</span>

<span class="comment"># LESSON: always start at the infrastructure layer. One NotReady node can look</span>
<span class="comment"># like three unrelated bugs if you triage bottom-up instead of top-down.</span></code></pre>
