                            <div class="eq-exp-label">Explanation</div>
                            <p>A production HA cluster needs more than just multiple masters. The key areas: (1) <strong>etcd quorum</strong> — odd number of members (3 or 5), (2) <strong>load balancer</strong> with health checks, (3) <strong>automated backups</strong>, (4) <strong>PDBs</strong> for critical workloads, (5) <strong>resource requests</strong> on all pods for proper scheduling, (6) <strong>certificate management</strong>, (7) <strong>RBAC</strong> and network policies. On the CKA, you're tested on individual pieces (etcd backup, PDBs, RBAC), but understanding how they fit together as a production readiness checklist shows mastery of the full stack.</p>
