            <section class="section-block" id="s36-1">
                <h3 class="section-h">36.1 Managed vs Self-Managed Kubernetes</h3>
                <span class="badge badge-concept">CONCEPT</span>
                <p>All three major cloud providers offer <strong>managed Kubernetes</strong> — they handle the control plane while you manage the worker nodes and workloads. Here's how they compare.</p>

                <div class="comparison-table">
                    <table>
                        <thead>
                            <tr>
                                <th>Feature</th>
                                <th>EKS (AWS)</th>
                                <th>GKE (Google)</th>
                                <th>AKS (Azure)</th>
                            </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Control Plane</strong></td>
                                <td>Managed ($0.10/hr)</td>
                                <td>Managed (free tier avail.)</td>
                                <td>Managed (free!)</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Worker Nodes</strong></td>
                                <td>Self-managed / Fargate</td>
                                <td>Standard / Autopilot</td>
                                <td>VMSS node pools</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Networking</strong></td>
                                <td>VPC CNI (AWS native)</td>
                                <td>VPC-native / Calico</td>
                                <td>Azure CNI / kubenet</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Load Balancer</strong></td>
                                <td>ALB / NLB</td>
                                <td>GCP TCP/HTTP LB</td>
                                <td>Azure LB / App GW</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Storage</strong></td>
                                <td>EBS CSI driver</td>
                                <td>PD CSI driver</td>
                                <td>Azure Disk CSI</td>
