            <div class="uth-body">
            <h5>🗺️ Managed Kubernetes — What the Cloud Provider Runs vs What You Run</h5>
            <p>EKS, GKE, and AKS don't just "host Kubernetes." They run the control plane for you while you manage worker nodes and workloads. Understanding the boundary is critical for CKA scenarios involving cloud clusters.</p>
