            <div class="info-box tip">
                <h5>💡 Renovate/Dependabot — the "no extra controller in your cluster" option</h5>
                <p>ArgoCD Image Updater and Flux image-reflector both run AS a controller inside (or beside) your cluster. Renovate and Dependabot take a different shape entirely: they run as a scheduled bot against your Git HOST (GitHub Actions, GitLab CI, or a hosted SaaS), scanning manifests for image references and opening a normal pull request when a newer tag exists — no cluster access, no extra CRDs, and the same PR-review workflow you already use for code. Many easypj-style teams prefer this for the manifest repo specifically: it keeps "who can write to Git" and "who can write to the cluster" as two completely separate concerns, and the diff a human reviews looks exactly like any other code-review PR.</p>
