            <div class="uth-callout"><strong>🔑 Image automation closes the LAST manual loop in "fully automated GitOps."</strong> Without it: CI builds an image, but a human still has to remember to bump the tag in the manifest repo. With it: the moment CI pushes a new tag, the bump-and-commit happens automatically, and your existing ArgoCD/Flux sync (which you've already set up for regular commits) ships it — the same reconciliation loop from the earlier "GitOps Reconciliation" diagram applies, unchanged.</div>

