                <div class="vs-prose">
                    <p><strong>In words:</strong> Chapter 39 closed the loop this guide has been building toward since Chapter 1's control-loop mental model — except now the "controller" (ArgoCD/Flux) reconciles the WHOLE cluster's manifests against Git, not just one Deployment's replica count. CI's job stops at "image pushed, manifest bumped"; GitOps takes it from there, forever, pulling instead of being pushed to.</p>
                    <p class="mb-0"><strong>The takeaway:</strong> Helm packages what you SHARE (chart repos, versioned releases with rollback); Kustomize patches what you OWN (base + overlays, no template language); GitOps consumes either one as a render step inside its sync loop. Rollback is always <code>git revert</code>, never a manual <code>kubectl</code> patch that selfHeal would just undo. This is the production stack every CKA-certified engineer runs the day after the exam.</p>
