                <div class="info-box warning">
                    <h5>⚠️ GOTCHA — a down aggregated APIService has a wider blast radius than its own group</h5>
                    <p>The apiserver periodically re-runs OpenAPI/discovery aggregation across EVERY registered APIService, including the ones nobody's actively querying. A hung (not just unreachable, but slow-to-timeout) aggregated apiserver can stall discovery for the WHOLE cluster for a few seconds — meaning <code>kubectl</code> commands that have nothing to do with <code>metrics.k8s.io</code> can feel sluggish while a broken metrics-server backend is timing out discovery calls in the background. This is why production clusters set tight <code>timeoutSeconds</code>-equivalent health checks on aggregated apiservers, and why a truly wedged aggregation layer (rare, but it happens after a bad custom-metrics-adapter deploy) is diagnosed the same way as §42.3's webhook wedge: <code>kubectl get apiservices</code> first, then decide whether to fix the backend or temporarily delete the offending <code>APIService</code> object to restore fast discovery.</p>
