            <p class="part-cover-lead">Passing the exam means you CAN operate a cluster; SRE practice means you operate it WELL. Up to this point, this guide has mostly been about MAKING easypj run on Kubernetes — Pods scheduled, Services routed, Ingress terminated, storage bound, RBAC enforced. Day-2 SRE is the discipline of KEEPING it running, and proving — with numbers — that it's healthy. This part goes beyond <code>kubectl top</code>: a real observability stack (the three pillars), alerting and SLOs in Chapter 43, then the multi-cluster, capacity, and cost concerns of running easypj at scale in Chapter 44.</p>
