            <div class="chapter-intro">
            <h2 class="chapter-title">Chapter 43 · Observability — Metrics, Logs, Traces, Alerts</h2>
            <p class="chapter-lead">
                You cannot operate what you cannot see. When <strong>easypj</strong> starts returning 500s on <code>/jobs/</code>,
                or page loads crawl, or a pod silently CrashLoops, the difference between a five-minute fix and a five-hour
                outage is whether you have <strong>metrics</strong> to spot it, <strong>logs</strong> to read it,
                <strong>traces</strong> to localize it, and <strong>alerts</strong> to wake you before the user does.
                Observability is how you turn "the site feels slow" into "the DB query in the JobPost list view jumped from
                8ms to 900ms at 14:03 when the Skills join lost its index."
            </p>

            <div class="chapter-meta">
                <span class="meta-tag">🔴 Advanced</span>
