            <div class="analogy-box">
                <h5>🧠 Real-World Analogy: The Car Dashboard</h5>
                <p><strong>Metrics</strong> are the gauges — speed, RPM, fuel, temperature — always-on numbers that tell you "how much / how fast / how hot," right now and over time. <strong>Logs</strong> are the event recorder — "at 14:03 the check-engine light came on" — a discrete, detailed record of one thing that happened. <strong>Traces</strong> are the trip computer breaking the journey into legs — "you spent 40 min on the highway, 5 min at the gas station, 20 min in traffic" — so you know exactly <em>where</em> the time went. <strong>Alerts</strong> are the warning chimes that fire when a gauge crosses a line you actually care about — not every flicker, just the ones that mean something.</p>
            </div>

