                        <summary>Show Answer</summary>
                        <pre><code class="language-bash"><span class="comment"># Wrong tool to blame — check metrics-server, not Prometheus</span>
kubectl get deploy metrics-server -n kube-system
<span class="comment"># 0/1 available → CrashLoopBackOff or Pending</span>

kubectl -n kube-system logs deploy/metrics-server
<span class="comment"># common cause: cert validation failing against kubelet on self-signed clusters</span>

<span class="comment"># fix (dev/self-signed clusters only — never on a real cluster with valid certs):</span>
kubectl -n kube-system patch deployment metrics-server --type=json \
  -p='[{"op":"add","path":"/spec/template/spec/containers/0/args/-","value":"--kubelet-insecure-tls"}]'</code></pre>
                        <div class="eq-explanation">
                            <div class="eq-exp-label">Explanation</div>
                            <p><strong>metrics-server</strong> is the lightweight, in-cluster, history-less source for <code>kubectl top</code> and the HPA — it is a completely separate component from Prometheus. Teams that only know "we run Prometheus" waste time checking the wrong stack; the fix is always in <code>kube-system</code>, not <code>easypj-production</code>.</p>
