                              │ group·dedupe·  │
                              │ silence·inhibit│ ◀── spend the ERROR BUDGET
                              └────────────────┘
</pre>
</div>
                <div class="vs-prose">
                    <p><strong>In words:</strong> easypj emits three signal types. <strong>Metrics</strong> are scraped by Prometheus (pull model) from <code>/metrics</code> on the pods, node-exporter, and kube-state-metrics into a local TSDB. <strong>Logs</strong> flow from stdout/stderr to Loki/EFK. <strong>Traces</strong> flow from the OTel SDK through a collector to Tempo/Jaeger. Grafana visualizes all three — RED for the web tier, USE for nodes/db — and exemplars let you jump from a metric spike straight to its trace.</p>
                    <p class="mb-0"><strong>The takeaway:</strong> Prometheus alerting rules — built on SLOs and burn rate, alerting on symptoms not causes — fire into Alertmanager, which groups, dedupes, silences and inhibits before paging Slack/PagerDuty/email. Every page spends part of the error budget (1 − SLO); when the budget is gone, you freeze risky changes until it recovers. That's the whole Day-2 observability loop this chapter builds — Chapter 44 asks how to run this same stack across a whole fleet of clusters without blowing the budget in a different sense: the bill.</p>
