            <p class="part-cover-lead">Knowing Kubernetes is necessary but not sufficient: the CKA is a <strong>speed + accuracy</strong> test under a 2-hour clock. Every previous part taught you a domain — Pods, Deployments, Services, storage, networking, security, cluster lifecycle, troubleshooting — and by now you can genuinely <strong>build</strong> a Kubernetes platform and host easypj on it. But the exam does not reward what you know; it rewards what you can <strong>finish, correctly</strong>, while a countdown timer burns in the corner of the screen. The gap between "I knew how to do that" and "I scored those points" is exactly what this part closes. Chapter 45 converts everything from Chapters 1–44 into a repeatable, point-maximizing exam process — and proves it works with a full 20-task timed simulator on the easypj/jobpost stack.</p>
