            <!-- ─────────── KEY TAKEAWAYS ─────────── -->
            <span class="ch-jump" id="ch45-takeaways"></span>
            <div class="key-takeaways">
                <h4>🔑 Key Takeaways</h4>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>The CKA is a 2-hour, hands-on SPEED + ACCURACY test (66% to pass).</strong> Most failures are process/time failures, not knowledge gaps — Chapters 1–44 already gave you the knowledge.</li>
                    <li><strong>Spend the first 5 minutes on the setup ritual</strong> — <code>k</code> alias + completion, <code>$do</code> (dry-run YAML) + <code>$now</code> (fast delete), 2-space expandtab vim, doc-search bookmarks in your head.</li>
                    <li><strong>Work 3 passes</strong> — quick wins (&lt;4m) → medium (5–8m) → hardest + verify. Never camp &gt;10 min on one task; never leave a question blank (partial credit is real and mechanically enforced by the grading pipeline).</li>
                    <li><strong>Switch CONTEXT and namespace every single question</strong> — this one habit alone prevents the single most expensive mistake on the exam.</li>
                    <li><strong>Generate YAML, don't hand-write it</strong> — <code>$do</code> for most objects, copied-and-adjusted skeletons from docs for NetworkPolicy/Ingress/Gateway API — and verify after every task with <code>get -o wide</code>, <code>describe</code>, <code>auth can-i</code>, or a <code>curl</code>.</li>
                    <li><strong>Grading is automated against live cluster state</strong> — exact names, namespaces and labels are non-negotiable, and sub-checks are graded independently, which is exactly why partial credit is real.</li>
                    <li><strong>The domain weights are not trivia — they're a budget.</strong> Troubleshooting (30%) deserves the most practice reps of any single domain; Storage (10%) deserves the least, proportionally.</li>
                    <li><strong>The 20-task simulator on easypj is your readiness gate.</strong> 75%+, self-scored honestly, means book the real exam.</li>
                </ul>
