                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number">Q6</span>
                    <div class="eq-question">What's the must-not-miss order for an etcd backup and restore?</div>
                    <details>
                        <summary>Show Answer</summary>
                        <div class="eq-answer-label">Answer</div>
                        <p>Snapshot save (with certs) → verify snapshot status → restore to a NEW data directory → repoint the etcd static-pod manifest at that new directory → verify objects return. Never restore over the live data directory.</p>
                        <div class="diagram-container">
                            <div class="diagram-title">The order that matters</div>
<div class="diagram-box">
<pre>
  save (with certs) → status (sanity check) → restore to NEW dir → repoint manifest
       │                                                                    │
       └───────────────────── never skip a step, never reorder ───────────┘
</pre>
</div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="eq-explanation">
                            <div class="eq-exp-label">Explanation</div>
                            <p>Restoring over a live directory risks a half-written, corrupted state with no way back — a fresh directory plus a manifest edit is safe and reversible.</p>
