        <section class="section-block" id="sb-1">
            <h3 class="section-h">B.1 Pod Template (with all common fields)</h3>
            <span class="badge badge-exam">📝 CKA EXAM</span>
            <p>The Pod is the atomic unit in Kubernetes. This template shows every field you'll encounter on the CKA exam.</p>

            <div class="cka-yaml-skeleton">
                <h4>Pod — Complete Exam Template</h4>
                <p class="skeleton-note">Fields marked with ← are most commonly tested on the CKA exam</p>
                <pre><code class="language-yaml">apiVersion: v1                          <span class="comment"># Always v1 for pods</span>
kind: Pod                               <span class="comment"># Object type</span>
metadata:
  name: easypj-web                      # ← Required: unique within namespace
  namespace: easypj                     # ← Omit for default namespace
  labels:                               # ← Key-value pairs for selection
    app: easypj
    tier: frontend
    version: v1
spec:
  securityContext:                      # ← Pod-level security (applies to every container)
    runAsNonRoot: true                  <span class="comment"># Refuse to start if the image would run as root (UID 0)</span>
    runAsUser: 1000                     # ← Numeric UID the process runs as
    fsGroup: 2000                       <span class="comment"># Group that owns files on mounted volumes</span>
  containers:                           # ← List of containers (at least 1)
  - name: web                           <span class="comment"># Container name</span>
    image: easypj:v1                    # ← Image[:tag]
    ports:
    - containerPort: 8000               <span class="comment"># Informational only — does NOT expose</span>
    env:                                # ← Environment variables
    - name: DEBUG
      value: "False"
    - name: DB_HOST
      valueFrom:
        configMapKeyRef:                # ← From ConfigMap
          name: easypj-config
          key: DB_HOST
    - name: SECRET_KEY
      valueFrom:
        secretKeyRef:                   # ← From Secret
          name: easypj-secret
          key: SECRET_KEY
    resources:                          # ← ALWAYS set in production
      requests:                         <span class="comment"># Scheduling guarantee</span>
        memory: "128Mi"
        cpu: "250m"
      limits:                           <span class="comment"># Hard ceiling</span>
        memory: "256Mi"
        cpu: "500m"
    securityContext:                    # ← Container-level (overrides pod-level on conflict)
      allowPrivilegeEscalation: false   <span class="comment"># Block sudo-style privilege gain inside the container</span>
      readOnlyRootFilesystem: true      # ← Root filesystem is read-only (mount emptyDir/PVC for any writes)
      capabilities:
        drop: ["ALL"]                   <span class="comment"># Drop every Linux capability, add back only what's needed</span>
    startupProbe:                       # ← Protects slow-starting apps from a premature liveness kill
      httpGet:
        path: /health
        port: 8000
      failureThreshold: 30              # ← 30 × periodSeconds (300s) before giving up and killing
      periodSeconds: 10
    readinessProbe:                     # ← When pod is ready for traffic
      httpGet:
        path: /health
        port: 8000
      initialDelaySeconds: 5
      periodSeconds: 10
    livenessProbe:                      # ← When to restart container
      httpGet:
        path: /health
        port: 8000
      initialDelaySeconds: 15
      periodSeconds: 20
    volumeMounts:                       # ← Mount volumes into container
    - name: app-data
      mountPath: /app/data
  volumes:                              # ← Define volumes at pod level
  - name: app-data
    persistentVolumeClaim:
      claimName: easypj-pvc
  restartPolicy: Always                 <span class="comment"># Always | OnFailure | Never</span>
  serviceAccountName: easypj-sa         # ← Explicit SA (security best practice)</code></pre>
