        <div class="info-box tip">
            <h5>🔑 Must-Remember Before the Exam</h5>
            <ul>
                <li><code>selector.matchLabels</code> is <strong>immutable</strong> on Deployments, StatefulSets, and Jobs once created — a mismatch or a later change means delete-and-recreate, not edit-in-place.</li>
                <li>Job/CronJob pod templates require <code>restartPolicy: OnFailure</code> or <code>Never</code> — <code>Always</code> (the Pod default) is rejected outright by the API server.</li>
                <li>Secret <code>data</code> is base64 — <strong>encoding, not encryption</strong>. Use <code>stringData</code> to skip the manual encode step, but it's still only base64 at rest without an <code>EncryptionConfiguration</code>.</li>
                <li>A default-deny NetworkPolicy on <code>Egress</code> <strong>must</strong> be paired with an allow-DNS-egress rule, or every in-cluster name lookup starts failing.</li>
                <li>HPA needs <strong>both</strong> metrics-server installed <strong>and</strong> CPU/memory <code>requests</code> set on the target pods — utilization is a percentage of the request, with nothing to compute against otherwise.</li>
                <li>StatefulSet needs a <strong>headless</strong> Service (<code>clusterIP: None</code>) named in <code>serviceName</code> — a normal ClusterIP Service there silently breaks stable per-pod DNS.</li>
                <li><code>WaitForFirstConsumer</code> on a StorageClass delays PV creation until a pod schedules, preventing the classic "volume node affinity conflict" zone-mismatch failure in multi-zone clusters.</li>
                <li>A CRD only adds a <em>type</em> — it does nothing on its own without a controller/operator actively watching and reconciling instances of that kind.</li>
                <li>A <code>ValidatingAdmissionPolicy</code> with no matching <code>ValidatingAdmissionPolicyBinding</code> enforces nothing — both objects are required together.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

