        <!-- ─────────── §C.2 ─────────── -->
        <section class="section-block" id="sc-2">
            <h3 class="section-h">C.2 The Deeper Triage Matrix: Symptom → First Command → Cause → Fix</h3>
            <p>The compact card above is for memory recall. This matrix is for when you're actually staring at a broken cluster and need to know <strong>exactly what to type first</strong>. Every row adds a <strong>FIRST COMMAND</strong> column — the single most information-dense command to run before you do anything else — plus several symptom classes the compact card leaves out entirely: a container that never starts because a referenced ConfigMap/Secret doesn't exist, a Service silently routing to nowhere, CoreDNS returning <code>NXDOMAIN</code> for a name that should resolve, an API server so dead that <code>kubectl</code> itself won't even connect, and an Ingress that returns 404s despite the pods behind it being perfectly healthy.</p>

            <div class="info-box tip">
                <h5>💡 Reading this table under pressure</h5>
                <p>Don't try to memorize all seventeen rows verbatim. Instead internalize the <em>pattern</em>: nearly every FIRST COMMAND is either <code>describe</code> (something is broken and Kubernetes already logged why, in the Events section) or a targeted <code>exec</code>/<code>run</code> probe from inside the cluster's network (something is broken between two things that both look "Ready" from the outside). If you can tell those two situations apart instantly, you can reconstruct most of this table from first principles even if your memory of the exact row goes blank.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="comparison-table">
                <table>
                    <thead>
                        <tr>
                            <th>Symptom</th>
                            <th>First Command</th>
                            <th>Likely Cause</th>
                            <th>Fix</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>CrashLoopBackOff</strong></td>
                            <td><code>kubectl logs &lt;pod&gt; --previous</code> + <code>describe</code></td>
                            <td>App crash / bad config / OOM</td>
                            <td>Fix config, probe, or dependency the app needs at startup</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>ImagePullBackOff / ErrImagePull</strong></td>
                            <td><code>kubectl describe pod</code> → Events</td>
                            <td>Wrong <code>image:tag</code> / no pull secret</td>
                            <td>Fix the image reference; add an <code>imagePullSecret</code></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>CreateContainerConfigError</strong></td>
                            <td><code>kubectl describe pod</code></td>
                            <td>Missing ConfigMap/Secret/key referenced by the pod spec</td>
                            <td>Create the missing ConfigMap/Secret, or fix the key name</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Pod Pending</strong></td>
                            <td><code>kubectl describe pod</code> → Events</td>
                            <td>No fitting resources / taint / affinity / no eligible node</td>
                            <td>Free resources, add tolerations, or fix affinity rules</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>PVC Pending</strong></td>
                            <td><code>kubectl describe pvc</code></td>
                            <td>No matching PV / wrong StorageClass / no provisioner</td>
                            <td>Create a matching PV, fix the storage class, or install the CSI driver</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>OOMKilled (exit 137)</strong></td>
                            <td><code>kubectl describe pod</code> → Last State</td>
                            <td>Memory limit set too low / genuine memory leak</td>
                            <td>Raise the memory limit, or fix the leak in the application</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Node NotReady</strong></td>
                            <td><code>ssh</code>; <code>systemctl status kubelet</code>; <code>journalctl -u kubelet</code></td>
                            <td>kubelet down / CNI missing / swap on / disk pressure</td>
                            <td>Start kubelet, install CNI, <code>swapoff -a</code>, or free disk space</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>FailedScheduling</strong></td>
                            <td><code>kubectl describe pod</code> → Events</td>
                            <td>Taint/affinity mismatch, or insufficient requested resources</td>
                            <td>Add matching tolerations, or fix the affinity/anti-affinity rules</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Forbidden (RBAC)</strong></td>
                            <td><code>kubectl auth can-i &lt;verb&gt; &lt;resource&gt; --as=&lt;subject&gt;</code></td>
                            <td>Missing Role/ClusterRole or the Binding that attaches it</td>
                            <td>Create the Role/ClusterRole plus its RoleBinding/ClusterRoleBinding</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Service: no endpoints</strong></td>
                            <td><code>kubectl get endpoints &lt;svc&gt;</code></td>
                            <td>Selector doesn't match pod labels, or no pods are Ready</td>
                            <td>Fix the selector to match pod labels; fix the readiness probe</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>connection refused</strong></td>
                            <td><code>get endpoints</code>; <code>exec curl</code> from a temp pod</td>
                            <td>Pod down / wrong <code>targetPort</code> / NetworkPolicy blocking</td>
                            <td>Fix the pod, the port mapping, or the NetworkPolicy rule</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>DNS NXDOMAIN</strong></td>
                            <td><code>exec nslookup</code> from a temp pod</td>
                            <td>CoreDNS down, or wrong FQDN/<code>ndots</code> assumption</td>
                            <td>Fix the CoreDNS Corefile / restart CoreDNS; use the fully-qualified name</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>certificate expired</strong></td>
                            <td><code>kubeadm certs check-expiration</code></td>
                            <td>Leaf certificate older than its ~1 year validity window</td>
                            <td><code>kubeadm certs renew all</code>; restart the control-plane static pods</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>etcd unavailable</strong></td>
                            <td><code>crictl ps/logs</code>; <code>etcdctl endpoint health</code></td>
                            <td>etcd down / cert problem / quorum lost</td>
                            <td>Fix the etcd static-pod manifest; restore from backup if data is corrupt</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>apiserver refused (kubectl is dead)</strong></td>
                            <td><code>crictl ps -a</code>; <code>crictl logs</code>; <code>journalctl -u kubelet</code></td>
                            <td>Bad apiserver static-pod manifest</td>
                            <td>Fix the manifest in <code>/etc/kubernetes/manifests/</code> — kubelet auto-restarts it</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Ingress not routing</strong></td>
                            <td><code>get ingress</code>; <code>get pods -n ingress-*</code></td>
