            <div class="info-box warning">
                <h5>⚠️ The mental model flip: no more kubectl</h5>
                <p>This is the single most disorienting failure mode in the entire troubleshooting domain because <strong>your primary tool stops working</strong>. Every instinct says "run <code>kubectl describe</code>" — but there is no API server to ask. The moment <code>kubectl get nodes</code> times out or refuses the connection, mentally switch from "control-plane API" mode to "container-runtime + systemd" mode: <code>crictl</code> talks directly to containerd/CRI-O, bypassing the API server entirely, and <code>journalctl -u kubelet</code> shows you what the kubelet itself is doing. Static pod manifests in <code>/etc/kubernetes/manifests/</code> are the one place you edit YAML directly on disk instead of via <code>kubectl apply</code> — the kubelet is watching that directory and will reconcile it for you.</p>
            </div>

