<span class="comment"># its STATUS column showing "Terminating" — the control plane accepted the</span>
<span class="comment"># delete but can't actually remove the Pod object from etcd yet.</span>
kubectl get pod easypj-worker -n easypj
<span class="comment"># NAME             READY   STATUS        RESTARTS   AGE</span>
<span class="comment"># easypj-worker    1/1     Terminating   0          45m</span>

<span class="comment"># 1. A deletionTimestamp being set but the object still present almost always</span>
<span class="comment">#    means a finalizer is blocking removal — list them:</span>
kubectl get pod easypj-worker -n easypj -o yaml | grep -A5 -E "finalizers|deletionTimestamp"
<span class="comment"># metadata:</span>
<span class="comment">#   deletionTimestamp: "2026-07-10T09:14:02Z"</span>
<span class="comment">#   finalizers:</span>
<span class="comment">#   - easypj.io/cleanup-volume        ← this finalizer is never being removed</span>

<span class="comment"># 2. Find out WHY the finalizer isn't clearing — usually a controller/operator</span>
<span class="comment">#    that owns that finalizer is down, crash-looping, or stuck on its own error:</span>
kubectl get pods -n easypj-operator
kubectl logs -n easypj-operator -l app=easypj-cleanup-controller --tail=50

<span class="comment"># 3. Also rule out a validating/mutating admission webhook silently rejecting</span>
<span class="comment">#    the finalizer-removal PATCH the controller is trying to send:</span>
kubectl get validatingwebhookconfigurations,mutatingwebhookconfigurations

<span class="comment"># 4a. PREFERRED fix — repair the owning controller/webhook so it actually</span>
<span class="comment">#     removes the finalizer itself (this is the only fully "safe" fix):</span>
kubectl rollout restart deployment/easypj-cleanup-controller -n easypj-operator

<span class="comment"># 4b. LAST RESORT ONLY — manually clear the finalizer. This skips whatever</span>
<span class="comment">#     cleanup that finalizer existed to guarantee (e.g. detaching a cloud</span>
<span class="comment">#     volume), so only do this once you've confirmed the cleanup already</span>
<span class="comment">#     happened or genuinely doesn't matter:</span>
kubectl patch pod easypj-worker -n easypj -p '{"metadata":{"finalizers":null}}' \
  --type=merge

<span class="comment"># 5. Confirm it's actually gone (not just re-created identically)</span>
kubectl get pod easypj-worker -n easypj</code></pre>
