                    <p>It's deliberately flat — one error, one command, no branching — because under time pressure you don't want to think, you want to <em>react</em>. Cover the right-hand column with your hand and quiz yourself on each error in the left column; once you can produce every FIRST COMMAND from memory without peeking, you've internalized the pattern well enough that you'll reach for the right command reflexively even for a symptom that isn't literally listed here. That's the real goal — not memorizing eighteen rows, but recognizing which <em>category</em> a new, never-seen-before symptom belongs to (workload / node / network / control-plane / RBAC) and knowing that category's default first move.</p>
